feat(audit): fact intake, batch-wide audit, and the finished component spec (M3.4-M3.5)

POST /facts -- an idempotent intake so a customer's own extractor can record facts
against dialogue the component already stores, without adopting the manager.  Two
properties make it safe to expose:
* idempotent: fact_id is "<summary_id>#<slot>" and the insert ignores an existing
  key, so a retry adds nothing (verified: second identical batch reports added=0,
  duplicates=1);
* verified BEFORE answering: the audit runs first, so a fact referencing a summary
  that does not exist comes back as an I1 violation and a value that never becomes
  visible comes back as I2.  This exposed a real boundary worth documenting rather
  than papering over: injecting a fact cannot *make* it visible, because the
  registry is derived from the summaries' fact_keys.  An external extractor must add
  facts to summaries whose text carries the value, and the endpoint tells it
  immediately when it has not.

audit_all() + GET /audit/summary -- the batch view.  Per-episode reports answer "is
this one sound"; a run needs the shape of the corpus (clean vs violating episodes,
which invariant is disappointing, outstanding erasure residue, extraction gaps),
because one violation in five hundred episodes is invisible in a mean.

Also in this change:
* GET /temporal (the versioned projection plus its consistency check and the DDL)
  and GET /history?slot=&upto_turn= on the sidecar;
* list_ledger_episodes() on the in-memory backend so audit_all covers it too;
* audit_check.py --aggregate prints the batch summary alongside the four controls;
* AUDIT.md rewritten as the finished component spec: five invariants (I1-I5) with
  what each needs to be checkable, the interface, the audit artifact, the measured
  results, the four controls that must fail, the compliance-erasure semantics, the
  temporal outsourcing contract, the sidecar surface, the boundaries, and an honest
  list of what is still missing.

Final regression: 101 tests; audit_check --aggregate (3 episodes clean, 0
violations, silent_loss_rate 0.0, all four controls firing); gate frontier unchanged
(42-45% on synthetic with 100% fact recall); 4-system hybrid run 8/8 rows; every
sidecar endpoint exercised over real HTTP including access control and idempotency.
